==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Atlantis Logistix''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ultra Atlantis Logistix''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit, though by no means a generalist, is still a formidable force versus Zombies, as its cheap cost and Insane Damage ability mesh well with cash-tight Zombie stages. Their subpar survivability (3 knockbacks and low range of 370, which still allows it to outrange many relevant Zombies) prevents it from being effective against Zombie enemies that burrow in front of them, but if summoned at the right time, they can make a huge difference by crippling or removing many threats outright.

What sets Mighty Aethur Ltd. apart from almost all other [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] and [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer Cats]] is its extreme negative Omni Strike coverage, reaching further than even [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Thermae]] (675<730), meaning that Mighty Aethur Ltd. can snipe unburrowed Zombies that have burrowed away from it.

Another merit of Mighty Aethur Ltd. is the [[Cat Transport (Combo)|Cat Transport]] combo with [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]], increasing worker start level by 2. This is one of the more efficient worker combos, equivalent to [[Longnecks (Combo)|Longnecks]] and only losing out to [[Don't Mess With Me! (Combo)|Don't Mess With Me!]] Considering how useful Courier is as a general attacker, Mighty Aethur Ltd. is still worth bringing even for the combo.

==='''True Form'''===
Ultra Atlantis Logistix gains improved survivability, though not from improved range or HP. Rather, this comes in the form of its 100% lethal strike survive and dodge chance. These contribute a lot to its survivability in general in Zombie-oriented stages, with dodge helping it slip hits in if Zombies ever bury into its range, and Survive giving this unit another chance in battle. You may invest in this True Form if you have the spare Catfruit to make this unit last longer against Zombies, or if you also wish to unlock its [[Talents]].

==='''Talents'''===
'''Soulstrike''' is surprisingly one of the best Talents on this unit, since unlike many other units in its set, Ultra Atlantis Logistix has a relatively short cooldown and a somewhat fast attack cycle, so it can afford staying behind if necessary while its negative Omni Strike catches Zombies from behind.

Ultra Atlantis Logistix gains the ability to '''Slow''', which is a nice bonus, though the uptime at max is only 33%. It's a nice bonus if you wish to prevent zombies like [[Cadaver Bear]] from pushing too far, though you should focus on other Talents first.

'''Immune to Weaken''' is fairly situational, as [[Zroco]] is the only Zombie that inflicts Weaken, and the chances of Logistix surviving being hit by multiple Zrocos without protection are low. It can help if it manages to reposition after being hit by Zroco, though again, matchups against threats that inflict it are generally poor.

'''Resist Freeze''', like other resist Talents, aren't worth the heavy investment. It may help against certain [[Henry]]+Zombie stages and against the likes of [[Zir Zeal]], though the Talent is very expensive to fully invest into and is generally not worth the investment.

As a unit reliant on stats, Attack Up is the second best Talent to invest in, next to Soulstrike, after investing [[Catseye]]s, of course. Health Up can be handy in some scenarios, though again it's more reliant on Survive and an inconsistent dodge rather than a stat-based ability like Resistant or Insanely tough, so its benefits are questionable at best.

